# Workspace instructions

Follow **[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)** at the repository root for all product, engineering, collaboration, and **MCP** defaults (including Context7 via `resolve-library-id` then `query-docs`).

Do not contradict `AGENTS.md`. Blog 3.0 ticket → code map: **[docs/blog-3-jira-conventions.md](../../docs/blog-3-jira-conventions.md)**. If something tool-specific is needed, keep it minimal here and expand only in `AGENTS.md`.

**Before building, read the ADRs.** Decisions are tool-agnostic and live in the register at **[docs/adr/README.md](../../docs/adr/README.md)** (e.g. ADR-005 component organization, ADR-006 design tokens) — the *same* canon Claude Code follows. Using Cursor never changes the rules; if a task would contradict an ADR, stop and flag it rather than diverging. See `AGENTS.md` § "Decision compliance".

## Preserve shared UI primitives (no preemptive changes)

- **UI design/build/plan:** read **[DESIGN.md](../../DESIGN.md)** first (composition + token names); values live in `@pakfactory/ui/globals.css`.
- **Scaffold / RSC / state:** read **[ENGINEERING.md](../../ENGINEERING.md)**; ADR index (domain + Applies to) at **[docs/adr/README.md](../../docs/adr/README.md)**.
- **Do not edit** existing components under [`packages/ui/src/components`](packages/ui/src/components) except when fixing a confirmed bug you were explicitly asked to fix.
- **CSS cascade:** follow **[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)** § UI and design system — `@pakfactory/ui/globals.css`, then the app’s `globals.css`, then component `className`. Spacing is **8pt**. App CSS may add a token only when ui does not define it; do not drive-by edit `packages/ui/src/globals.css` for a single feature.
- **Allowed exception:** **add** new primitive files only when required (e.g. from the shadcn CLI)—additive only.
- **Do not change** global shell layout (root `layout.tsx`, navbar) unless the task explicitly asks.
- **Doc map:** [`docs/ai-agent-docs.md`](../../docs/ai-agent-docs.md) — keep Cursor digests thin; do not restate AGENTS.
